# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your real Firebase project's web
# config (Firebase console → Project settings → Your apps → SDK setup and
# configuration). These values are NOT secret — Firebase web config is meant
# to be public; access control is enforced entirely by firestore.rules.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# Set to "true" to route the app at the local Firestore/Auth emulators
# instead of your real Firebase project — used for all local development.
VITE_USE_EMULATORS=false
